<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giacomo Matteotti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1885–1924</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giacomo Matteotti was an Italian socialist politician, secretary of the Unitary Socialist Party. In May 1924 he denounced violence and fraud in the elections in a speech to the Chamber of Deputies; on 10 June he was kidnapped and murdered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> by Fascist squad members. The crisis that followed led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> to suppress the opposition and establish an open dictatorship from 1925.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giacomo-matteotti.jpg" alt="Giacomo Matteotti" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giacomo_Matteotti_2_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
